1) Config do Task Scheduler (a tua tela está quase certa ✅)

Na task \eMatch Automation\RunEMatchDesktop:

Program/script
C:\Windows\System32\cmd.exe
Add arguments
/c call "D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\RunEMatchDesktop.bat"
Start in
D:\Projects\eMatchStarters

Regras importantes ⚠️

Usa /c (senão o cmd fica aberto e “não faz nada”)
Usa call (senão pode matar o fluxo e não propagar exit code)
O BAT da task não é vazio. Ele é o “runner” que lê o contexto e executa.
2) BAT correto (com quebras de linha e espaçamento ✅)

Cria este arquivo exatamente aqui:

D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\RunEMatchDesktop.bat
@echo off
setlocal EnableExtensions EnableDelayedExpansion

set "CTX_FILE=D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\run-context.properties"
if not exist "%CTX_FILE%" exit /b 2

for /f "usebackq tokens=1* delims==" %%A in ("%CTX_FILE%") do (
  set "K=%%A"
  set "V=%%B"
  if not "!K!"=="" set "!K!=!V!"
)

if "%WORKSPACE%"=="" exit /b 3
if "%PROJECT_FILE%"=="" exit /b 3
if "%KATALON_EXE%"=="" exit /b 3
if "%COLLECTION_PATH%"=="" exit /b 3

set "REPORTS_DIR=%WORKSPACE%\Reports"
if not exist "%REPORTS_DIR%" mkdir "%REPORTS_DIR%" >nul 2>&1

set "MARKER=%REPORTS_DIR%\__jenkins_task_exitcode.txt"
if exist "%MARKER%" del /f /q "%MARKER%" >nul 2>&1

set "LOG_DIR=D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\logs"
if not exist "%LOG_DIR%" mkdir "%LOG_DIR%" >nul 2>&1

for /f %%T in ('powershell -NoProfile -Command "Get-Date -Format yyyyMMdd_HHmmss"') do set "TS=%%T"
set "LOG_FILE=%LOG_DIR%\katalon_%TS%.log"

echo [INFO] WORKSPACE=%WORKSPACE%>>"%LOG_FILE%"
echo [INFO] PROJECT_FILE=%PROJECT_FILE%>>"%LOG_FILE%"
echo [INFO] COLLECTION_PATH=%COLLECTION_PATH%>>"%LOG_FILE%"
echo [INFO] BROWSER_TYPE=%BROWSER_TYPE%>>"%LOG_FILE%"
echo [INFO] RETRY=%RETRY%>>"%LOG_FILE%"
echo [INFO] REPORTS_DIR=%REPORTS_DIR%>>"%LOG_FILE%"

"%KATALON_EXE%" -noSplash -runMode=console -consoleLog ^
  -projectPath="%WORKSPACE%\%PROJECT_FILE%" ^
  -retry=%RETRY% ^
  -testSuiteCollectionPath="%COLLECTION_PATH%" ^
  -browserType="%BROWSER_TYPE%" ^
  -reportFolder="%REPORTS_DIR%" ^
  1>>"%LOG_FILE%" 2>&1

set "EC=%ERRORLEVEL%"
echo %EC%>"%MARKER%"

exit /b %EC%

